177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 95 0 R
/E (      Throughout this project, I significantly refined my inquiry to create the best possible player experience. I started by shifting the focus from control instability to translating physical sensory experiences and finally applied alterbiography to create feelings that players could interpret and create in their own way. I learned that game mechanics must be continuously questioned and iterated to better serve the player experience. For example, I asked myself if a button mashing system truly allows players to interpret the game in their own way, and what if we switched to a typing system that allows for more diverse interpretations. This iterative process reinforced that translating psychological states into physical sensory experience is not only possible through mechanics, but requires the cohesion of visuals, sound, and design working together. Moving forward, I want to let others playtest the game, refine it, and improve it smoothly before continuing with the remaining stages in Studio 3.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
